WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:08.504
In this final video, we put everything
together by following every cable of one TPU

2
00:00:08.504 --> 00:00:08.944
rack.

3
00:00:10.294 --> 00:00:17.304
We will trace one rack's cables, follow one
fiber from the switch all the way to a spine,

4
00:00:17.304 --> 00:00:23.606
review the done-when checklists, and list the
open items to ask your lead about.

5
00:00:27.756 --> 00:00:30.956
We will follow TPU rack 504.

6
00:00:32.156 --> 00:00:35.377
Split the number: row five, spot four.

7
00:00:36.127 --> 00:00:43.125
Spot four is north of the middle aisle, so it
is served by end of row rack 511.

8
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:46.243
Row five is in pod ten.

9
00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:51.774
511 serves racks 502 to 510.

10
00:00:52.524 --> 00:01:00.060
Using the guide's rule, the lowest-numbered
rack goes on the bottom row, so 504 is the

11
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.127
third rack: row three on the panel.

12
00:01:03.877 --> 00:01:06.031
Confirm that on the cutsheet.

13
00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:17.792
Its OCS cables go to pod ten's SPOCS racks:
red to 512, orange to 612, yellow to 712.

14
00:01:21.942 --> 00:01:26.443
Here is every cable on rack 504 in one table.

15
00:01:27.193 --> 00:01:30.052
Pause the video to study it if you like.

16
00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:42.352
The 144-fiber trunk runs from the switch's odd
ports to row three on the front of 511's

17
00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:42.993
panel.

18
00:01:44.343 --> 00:01:53.681
Behind row three, 511's eight 192-fiber trunks
carry it to the eight patch panel racks, all

19
00:01:53.681 --> 00:02:00.557
in the RU thirty-five panel, slot three,
columns C and D, lane one.

20
00:02:01.907 --> 00:02:12.659
The three OCS cables go to 512, 612 and 712,
with the same X and X plus one on every slot.

21
00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:21.539
The six copper runs go to 511's panels at RU
twenty-four, thirty and twenty-two.

22
00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:30.953
And 511 itself is a standard end of row rack,
so its management trunks are twelve fiber.

23
00:02:35.103 --> 00:02:42.731
Now let us follow a single fiber leg, leg one
of rack 504's trunk, all the way to the

24
00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:43.359
spines.

25
00:02:44.559 --> 00:02:46.138
Leg one is blue.

26
00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:53.117
Two times one, minus one: it plugs into port
one of the top of rack switch.

27
00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:59.459
At 511, it lands in column A, port one, row
three.

28
00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:02.385
Label A1 dash 3.

29
00:03:03.735 --> 00:03:09.581
Behind that port is the column A 192-fiber
trunk.

30
00:03:10.331 --> 00:03:17.563
Row three holds legs five and six, and the odd
leg, five, sits right behind A1.

31
00:03:18.313 --> 00:03:23.305
Column A from a spot eleven rack goes to rack
107.

32
00:03:24.655 --> 00:03:33.017
At 107, that trunk lands in the RU thirty-five
panel, in columns C and D, lane one.

33
00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:38.311
Leg five is odd, so it sits in column C, row
three.

34
00:03:39.661 --> 00:03:47.473
The C and D module in row three mixes this
trunk with its neighbor in lane two, which is

35
00:03:47.473 --> 00:03:52.888
611, and sends four cords to spines one, two,
three and four.

36
00:03:54.238 --> 00:03:55.667
Path complete.

37
00:03:56.417 --> 00:04:03.396
One leg, followed from the TPU rack, through
the end of row rack and the patch panel, to

38
00:04:03.396 --> 00:04:04.268
the spines.

39
00:04:08.418 --> 00:04:11.575
Each guide ends with a done-when checklist.

40
00:04:12.325 --> 00:04:13.968
Here are the highlights.

41
00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:19.326
The full lists are in lesson fifteen and in
the reference guide.

42
00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:28.319
At the TPU rack: sixteen legs in the odd
ports, spares dressed off the floor, the three

43
00:04:28.319 --> 00:04:35.843
OCS cables in their port groups, six copper
runs, and everything scoped and labeled.

44
00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:44.645
For OCS cables: the right color to the right
SPOCS rack, the legs in their slots, the same

45
00:04:44.645 --> 00:04:51.103
X everywhere, the split point in the right
place, and the right dressing side.

46
00:04:52.453 --> 00:05:00.367
For copper and management: jack number equals
port number, the right trunk size on the right

47
00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:07.679
positions, SPOCS cords at spots eleven and
thirteen, and the spine end patched before

48
00:05:07.679 --> 00:05:08.367
turn-up.

49
00:05:09.717 --> 00:05:18.312
For the large trunks: one TPU rack per front
row, one 192-fiber trunk per rear column, two

50
00:05:18.312 --> 00:05:25.952
different end of row trunks in every module,
and the correct module part number.

51
00:05:30.102 --> 00:05:32.449
Finally, the open items.

52
00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:39.172
These are places where the guide disagrees
with itself, or simply does not say.

53
00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:41.671
Bring them to your lead.

54
00:05:42.671 --> 00:05:48.175
The cover says revision D, but every page
footer says revision C.

55
00:05:48.925 --> 00:05:51.315
Make sure you have the current revision.

56
00:05:52.665 --> 00:06:00.634
Bend radius: the guide's fifteen times is not
on any DRS so far, and the tray drawings show

57
00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:07.641
more than twenty times while the general sheet
allows ten times without tension.

58
00:06:08.391 --> 00:06:13.553
The DRS is the requirement; confirm the number
with your lead.

59
00:06:14.903 --> 00:06:21.111
The copper tray tier: tier two in most places,
tier one on page fourteen.

60
00:06:22.461 --> 00:06:30.056
The OCS spare legs, and the twelve versus
twenty-four fiber trunks on the BMS racks.

61
00:06:31.406 --> 00:06:36.803
The shuffle module part number, and the number
of SPOCS uplinks per trunk.

62
00:06:38.153 --> 00:06:45.950
And details the guide does not cover at all,
like which rack is which TPU number, copper

63
00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:50.292
and fiber testing, and where the FB0 switch
sits.

64
00:06:54.442 --> 00:06:58.026
You have now followed every cable path in the
hall.

65
00:06:58.776 --> 00:07:02.723
When you are ready, take the final assessment
in the course.

66
00:07:03.473 --> 00:07:08.998
Your results are shown by topic, so you will
know exactly what to review.

67
00:07:09.748 --> 00:07:16.617
Have the current DRS on hand for every task,
and keep the reference guide with you too.

68
00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:23.767
Remember: the DRS says how, and the cutsheet
is the final word on any port.

69
00:07:24.517 --> 00:07:26.779
When in doubt, stop and ask.

